dialect protocol
protocol stdio.stl.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.stl
start record

# P2-FG1-FIX: REAL binary op frame, replacing the prior `print_stl_op(self).into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut (`../🦀️component.rs`'s upgraded `OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op`,
# `#region 🔖️OpBinaryCodec`) — per this wave's own findings, `stl` was one of 4 stdio standards
# still on that shortcut despite `md`'s sibling `stdio.md.mutations` protocol already completing
# the real-binary-frame upgrade this same wave (`format u8` + `tag u8` header, same pattern
# retyped here).
#
# `StlMutation` is a genuine data-carrying enum (6 variants; `SetSnapshot`/`InsertTriangle`/
# `SetTriangleVertices` embed `StlSnapshot`/`StlTriangle`/`[[f64;3];3]`) — no `DslField` impl
# exists for a data-carrying enum (blanket impls cover only ints/bool/String/Vec<T: DslField>/
# BTreeMap/[T;N]/DslValue/Wire, never a data-carrying enum), so the generic `format u8 | ordinal
# varint | record body` layout (`pack_rt::encode_record_body`/`dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`,
# both requiring a `RecordSpec` derived FROM a `DslField` impl) genuinely does not fit — confirmed
# by re-reading the type, not assumed (same structural blocker this artifact's own `StlMutation`
# doc comment cites). Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`
# convention) + `tag u8` (the `StlMutation` variant's declaration-order ordinal, 1=`SetSnapshot` ..
# 6=`SetTriangleVertices` — `NoMutation` was dropped, ordinal 0 retired, not reassigned) as two
# REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain.
#
# `StlMutation`'s payload tree has ZERO self-recursion (same as its `StlDiff` sibling — see
# `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`'s own doc comment for the full citation), so
# every payload field is real fixed/varint binary at the RUST layer (`write_varint_u64` for
# `index: usize`, `enc_vec3_bin`/`enc_vertices_bin`/`enc_triangle_bin`/`enc_snapshot_bin` for the
# rest — never text-as-binary). Only `SetSnapshot`'s `Vec<StlTriangle>` keeps the payload opaque at
# THIS protocol-dialect layer: a variable-length vector-of-records hits the same
# `protocol-array-of-records` `walk_protocol` gap the sibling diff protocol file documents
# (non-blocking `mechanism_gaps` entry, filed once, applies to both facets).
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
